v1.18.0
INFRA-1559 deploy-apps deploys the app IDs in DEPLOY_APP_IDS when it is set and keeps its own change detection when it is not

Previously:
- INFRA-1467 push a shared Docker image under each Kubernetes app name that uses it, since Kubernetes pods pull an image named after the app
- INFRA-1076 attribute a fleet-merge deploy to the run owner (the Co-authored-by trailer) and fall back to the fleet bot; detect fleet merges by the clever-fleet[bot] commit author, not the message body
- Namespace the pr-review skill invocation and allow the Skill tool, so the claude-code action runs Clever's review instead of Claude's built-in one
- INFRA-1076 make CI bot-tolerant: attribute a fleet-merge deploy (detected by the clever-fleet[bot] co-author trailer) to the fleet bot, and skip the CI-failure notify for bot authors instead of failing the job
- Make the shared pr-review skill the only review path, dropping the inline prompt and @claude-beta gate
- Error when apps share a Dockerfile path but publish different artifacts
- Route @claude-beta reviews through the shared pr-review skill
- Support repos with no launch.yaml
- Move k8s deploys to platform events
